# Nothing here is needed to try the app: `npm run dev` creates two development users
# (daniel / vee, password "dev") and keeps its data in ./.data.
#
# For a real deployment, run `npm run setup:auth` and set the three values it prints as environment
# variables (Netlify: Site configuration -> Environment variables). Never commit them.
#
# SIGNAL_USERS=[{"id":"...","name":"Daniel","hash":"pbkdf2$sha256$310000$..."},{"id":"...","name":"Vee","hash":"..."}]
# SIGNAL_SESSION_SECRET=at-least-32-random-characters
# SIGNAL_ADMIN_TOKEN=at-least-32-random-characters

# Optional: expose the backend-free 3D scene preview (#/scene-preview) in a production build.
# VITE_ENABLE_SCENE_PREVIEW=1
